    {
      "id": "C03-04",
      "subtitles_zh": "这支分队的六个兵团也完整核对过，身份和满员数没变，人数变化能逐团对上。规则先算整军预算，再按符合条件的兵团顺序分配整数。这一例恰好也能与各团比例取整吻合，但不能推广成所有兵团永远各自独立乘百分比。",
      "subtitles_en": "All six regiments were checked, with identities and maximum strengths unchanged. Their soldier changes reconcile individually. The rule first calculates an army-wide budget, then distributes integer losses to eligible regiments in order. This example also happens to match percentages rounded down separately for each regiment. That does not mean every regiment always receives its own independent percentage calculation.",
